{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"certifiable":true,"criteria":[{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":247,"line_start":232,"path":"AGENTS.md"},"criterion":"Agent guidance (AGENTS.md) states that any background load generator or long-running helper a subagent spawns must be bounded in wall-clock time AT SPAWN, not merely killed at the end.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":259,"line_start":249,"path":"AGENTS.md"},"criterion":"The guidance gives a copy-pasteable bounded pattern (`timeout 120 python -c '...' &`) and a process-group teardown (`trap 'kill 0' EXIT INT TERM`), with one line on why an unbounded loop outlives harness death.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":268,"line_start":261,"path":"AGENTS.md"},"criterion":"The guidance forbids leaving PPID-1 orphans: a subagent reaps what it spawned before returning, including on error paths.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":50,"line_start":1,"path":"scripts/check_orphaned_load.py"},"criterion":"A detection check reports compute processes whose parent is PID 1 and whose accumulated CPU time exceeds 3600 CPU-seconds by default, overridable via --min-cpu-seconds. Runnable as a plain command with no CI-provider dependency.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":60,"line_start":1,"path":"tests/scripts/test_check_orphaned_load.py"},"criterion":"The check flags a bounded decoy process it is given and does NOT flag a normally-parented process.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":220,"line_start":200,"path":"scripts/check_orphaned_load.py"},"criterion":"The check's process-inspection seam is injectable so the test never depends on real system process state or on spawning a real long-lived CPU burner.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":148,"line_start":130,"path":"tests/scripts/test_check_orphaned_load.py"},"criterion":"The real (non-injected) adapter is exercised at least once against live process state in a READ-ONLY smoke assertion.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":294,"line_start":276,"path":"AGENTS.md"},"criterion":"An operator note documents how to reclaim an already-leaked batch (pkill -f 'while True: pass') and where the guidance lives.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":240,"line_start":185,"path":"tests/scripts/test_check_orphaned_load.py"},"criterion":"System-owned executables are excluded by default, with --include-system to opt back in. A test asserts a system-path record is filtered by default and reported under --include-system.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":302,"line_start":232,"path":"AGENTS.md"},"criterion":"Bug 'Agent-spawned CPU load generators leak as PPID-1 orphans and run unbounded for days' is actually resolved: the reported defect no longer reproduces and expected behavior holds.","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true}],"findings":[],"material_fingerprint":null,"metrics":{"alias_index_build_ms":577,"commits_inspected":2796,"descendant_ids":0,"descendant_scope_ms":1427,"det_ms":3245.9,"diff_validation_ms":110,"distinct_references":2332,"git_history_read_ms":116,"landing_check_ms":834,"llm_calls":1,"llm_ms":86143.2,"material_policy_ms":0,"pre_verifier_total_ms":4863,"referencing_commits_found":1,"requests":14,"structural_scan_ms":2483,"ticket_ref_resolution_ms":25,"tool_calls":15,"total_ms":89440.4,"verifier_annotation_ms":0,"verifier_attempt_count":1,"verifier_attempt_setup_ms":1,"verifier_attempts_ms":212375,"verifier_